# Add new changelog entries following the format below.
# Add newest entries to the top of the list.
# Separate entries from eachother with a blank line.
#
# Alternatively, if your changelog is automatically generated (e.g. with
# the git-change-log command provided with Sailfish OS SDK), create a
# harbour-find-my-device.changes.run script to let mb2 run the required commands for you.

# * date Author's Name <author's email> version-release
# - Summary of changes

* Tue Jul 30 2026 Dominik Heidinger <dominikh@atomicmail.io> 2.0-1
- CHANGED: Harbour/Jolla-Store compliance refactoring (two-RPM model)
- CHANGED: App now runs sandboxed (Sailjail) with stock permissions
  Internet;Location;Audio;Downloads
- CHANGED: Daemons, privileged helper and systemd units moved into the new
  harbour-find-my-device-daemon package (bundled in the app RPM; in-app
  sideload install from the Settings page, or separate install via
  OpenRepos/Chum)
- CHANGED: Daemons run permanently and steer themselves via the shared DB
  (settings generation counter + heartbeats); no systemd control from the GUI
- CHANGED: Foreground GPS fix now uses QtPositioning (QML PositionSource)
  instead of dbus/gi in the app process
- CHANGED: Ringtone preview now plays via QtMultimedia in QML
- CHANGED: App data moved to the Sailjail data dir
  ~/.local/share/harbour-find-my-device/harbour-find-my-device/ (old DB and
  photos are migrated automatically)
- ADDED: Degraded mode - the app is fully usable without the daemon package;
  daemon-dependent switches are greyed out and offer the install flow
- ADDED: Daemon status/version from DB heartbeats incl. in-app update hint
- ADDED: CI builds both RPMs (daemon first) and gates the app RPM with the
  official sdk-harbour-rpmvalidator; Chum metadata prepared in both specs
- FIX: MQTT publishing now survives WLAN/mobile network handovers: publishes
  are verified (PUBACK) and repaired via forced reconnect + republish; the
  GPS daemon connects per tick instead of holding a stranded connection and
  keeps an undeliverable fix pending for the next cycle
- FIX: TCP_USER_TIMEOUT ends the minutes-long retransmit phases on half-open
  sockets; command daemon reconnects instantly on ConnMan network changes;
  UI client detects handovers via a source-address check
- FIX: battery use reduced - daemon sleep loops wake ~2x/min instead of 1x/s,
  TCP keepalive probing on idle connections reduced to a fifth
- FIX: Moved background-daemon banner from top to bottom due to hardware-notches.

* Sun Jul 26 2026 Dominik Heidinger <dominikh@atomicmail.io> 1.1-1
- FIX: Improve MQTT connection robustness across WLAN/mobile handovers
- FIX: Add rotating file logs under /tmp/
- ADDED: Enhancement of descriptions and texts.
- ADDED: french translation provided by @EnigmaTriton

* Tue Jul 21 2026 Dominik Heidinger <dominikh@atomicmail.io> 1.0-1
- ADDED: swedish translation provided by @eson57
- FIX: daemon_cmd - in some cases false user was picked for wipe of device.
- FIX: Added detailed description why sailjail needs to be off.
- FIX: Switched dbus services to freedesktop.systemd api
- FIX: mqtt client was not closed when publish was changed to 0
- FIX: Long delay for first FIX after appstart
- ADDED: Show bannner when GPS FIX was not successfully after 90s.
- FIX: GPS-Daemon starts to connect to MQTT now on startup and not after GPS-FIX.

* Tue Jul 14 2026 Dominik Heidinger <dominikh@atomicmail.io> 0.1-1
- Initial implementation of application
- Added MainPage, Device-Page, Map-Page, Settings-Page
- Added backend logic for device tracking, commands, and settings management
